id: mental-model:dave:ai-talk-in-the-park
title: "Dave / AI talk in the park"
kind: mental-model
record_shape: header
status: draft
spec_version: mental-model.v0.1
template_ref: templates/mental-model.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-13; from Dave's spoken rehearsal of the talk and the reflection he pasted; the plan is his, the dates and shares are the bot's proposals"
arena: "A Parker, Colorado park, one Saturday morning this fall, for one hour, with neighbours on blankets"
objective_ref: dave/ai-talk-in-the-park/objective-holon.yawn
runtime_ref: "https://yawn.bot/dave/ai-talk-in-the-park"
work_order_ref: "yawn-ai/yawn.bot YAWNS/WorkOrders/AI_TALK_IN_THE_PARK_2026_09_13.yawn"
updated: 2026-09-13

questions:
  - key: role
    answer: "Speaker Dave. The scope on duty for one hour on the grass: transfer presence, say only what I would say to a neighbour, and hand parents the chain."
  - key: relevance
    answer: >
      Because my kids are four and five and the world they are walking into is
      one nobody can see. The talk is how I find the other parents who feel
      that, and how I practice saying it plainly enough that a five-year-old
      could follow.
  - key: definition
    answer: "A free, quiet hour in a Parker park where I talk about raising small kids into a world where AI is arriving, and I start with a yawn."
  - key: inside
    answer: "The yawn as the shared, unexplained thing; the chain a child can carry; the game you are playing right now; who is speaking; where and when; what my bot does and does not do."
  - key: show
    answer: "A blanket. The first yawn, mine. One question at a time."
  - key: assumptions
    answer: "That presence transfers in an hour; that the Town's permit path is as reported; that parents are the audience; that the bot's candidate dates are close enough to start from."
  - key: proof
    answer: "A rental or permit in hand, a date, people on blankets, and what they did next."
  - key: lacuna
    answer: "The Town's answer, the date, whether anyone gives, and whether presence transfers at all."

concept:
  name: AI talk in the park
  one_line: "One hour on the grass, starting from a yawn, about raising small kids into a world where AI is arriving."
  inside:
    - name: "the yawn"
      glyph: "( o )"
      one_line: "the one thing everyone here does and nobody can fully explain; where presence starts"
    - name: "the chain"
      glyph: "o-o-o-o"
      one_line: "you are an organism, you have needs, you weigh, predict, choose, find out, and live with it; true in every future"
    - name: "the game"
      glyph: "|||"
      one_line: "which scope is running right now, and so which standards are on duty"
    - name: "the blanket"
      glyph: "[___]"
      one_line: "the whole setup: no amplifier, no vendor, nobody has to stay"
    - name: "the town"
      glyph: "^"
      one_line: "a permit or a rental, a park, a Saturday; the part that is not mine to decide alone"

show:
  - icon: "blanket"
    do: "Sit down before you speak. Let people arrive."
    say: "What is one thing every person here does that none of us can explain?"
  - icon: "yawn"
    do: "Go first. Yawn in front of everyone, then wait."
    say: "Could you think about anything else while that happened?"
  - icon: "question"
    do: "Ask the one question, then stop talking."
    say: "What game are you playing right now, and which of your standards are on duty in it?"

embody:
  - "Say only what you would say on the grass to a neighbour. If it needs the transcript to make sense, it is not ready."
  - "Label the prediction as a prediction and the hope as a hope. Robots in Parker in two years is a prediction; a hundred people on blankets is a hope."
  - "When someone asks why it is called yawn, answer with the yawn, not with the product."
  - "Never book, send, or collect on Dave's behalf without his press; draft, address, and wait."
  - "The talk's questions are ranked by what a parent needs first, not by what Dave finds most interesting."

assumptions:
  - text: "Presence can be transferred to a group in one hour, starting from a shared yawn."
    epistemic_status: assumed
  - text: "A gathering of ten or more on Town property needs a Community Event Permit, and park shelters are reserved through the Parks and Recreation rental request."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "Parents orienting on behalf of a child are the audience that will come back."
    epistemic_status: inferred
  - text: "The three candidate Saturdays and the twenty-to-fifty sizing are close enough to start the conversation with the Town."
    epistemic_status: assumed
  - text: "What Dave said for the speech about himself is his to publish; what he marked as not for the speech is not."
    epistemic_status: reported

proof:
  covers:
    - questions
    - show
    - embody
  signals:
    - "The Town answers with a path, a fee, and an open Saturday."
    - "A date is chosen by Dave and written into the work order, not by the bot."
    - "People on blankets, counted, and one thing each did afterward."
    - "scripts/validate-mental-models.mjs passes on this record and its page."
  falsifier: "If the bot books a park, sends the outreach, or collects money without Dave's press, or if the talk happens and nobody can say what changed for them afterward, this model is not being honoured."
  not_covered:
    - "concept: the glyphs are a View choice, not a claim"
    - "assumptions: each is labelled and waits on its own evidence"
  status: seed-backed

lacunae:
  - "The Town of Parker's answer: rental or permit, tier, fee, deposit, lead time."
  - "The date and the park."
  - "Whether a donation rail should exist, and for what stated use."
  - "Whether presence transfers, and how anyone would know."

sources:
  - text: "Dave's spoken rehearsal of the talk in a Claude Code session on 2026-09-13, and the reflection he pasted to reconstruct a lost eureka; retained in that session, hashed in the runtime's public/dave/model.yawn."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "Town of Parker Community Event Permits (parkerco.gov/2445) and Parks and Recreation park rentals (parkerrec.com/219), as summarized by search results on 2026-09-13; the pages themselves were not reachable from the session."
    epistemic_status: reported
  - text: "core/entity-and-coupling.yawn: the settled role that this talk sits under (steward of yawn.bot, so that the bills are paid and agency stays high)."
    epistemic_status: observed
